B.a4l=new A.cy("What is this tool?","Calculates the remaining serviceable life of the Number 1 and Number 2 starter generator brush sets, per the detailed inspection procedure (39-A-24-31-01-01A-31AA-A).",null)
B.a4p=new A.cy("Aircraft & generator identification","Optionally record the aircraft registration, each generator's serial number, and free-text comments. These are included in the shared/downloaded PDF but do not affect the calculation.",null)
B.a4E=new A.cy("1 \u2014 Measure the shortest brush","Find the shortest brush in the set and measure its length (Y). A new brush is 17.78 mm (0.7 in) long.\n\nTip: scroll wheel on the field to adjust the value.",null)
B.a4o=new A.cy("2 \u2014 Enter operated hours","Enter the brush operated hours (T) from the Aircraft Log Book.",null)
B.a4w=new A.cy("3 \u2014 Visual checks","Tick any box that applies after examining the brush with a strong light: damaged, cracked, or seated area unsatisfactory (below 85% minimum, per detail C/D of the IETP figure). Any of these alone requires discarding the brush set.",null)
B.a4z=new A.cy("4 \u2014 Read the result","Brush wear (X) = 17.78 \u2212 Y.\nWear rate (Z) = X \xf7 T.\nServiceable life (W) = Y \xf7 Z.\n\nThe brush set is flagged for discard if any visual check is ticked, or if the calculated serviceable life is below 150 hours.",null)
B.a4r=new A.cy("5 \u2014 Share PDF","Once at least one generator has valid inputs, download/share buttons appear. They generate a PDF report with both generators' results.",null)
B.a4T=new A.cy("Safety","Always refer to up-to-date official AW139 maintenance publications before performing any maintenance action. This tool is for reference only.",null)
